{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1495478-help-with-a-navajo-pantheon","id":1495478,"title":"Help with a Navajo Pantheon","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-10-23T07:53:05-07:00","id":1495478,"title":"Help with a Navajo Pantheon","content":"I'm running an origin game where the players do not even know the game SCION exists. They are a group of people who are estranged from at least one parent for most of their life. Next game they will have their visitations. At which point, I will break the fourth wall and hand them the book allowing them to rewrite their characters.<br /> <br /> One of my players/characters is intensely interested in Navajo culture and art. However, neither of us is well-versed in the mythology of the Navajo.<br /> <br /> Has anyone found good homebrew that might have that prepackaged for me?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27242-ravynwinter","name":"Ravynwinter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-23T16:57:10-07:00","id":1495501,"title":"","content":"I have not yet had a chance to read either of these, so I can't testify to their quality, but I have them on my list for future reading and research:<br /> Navaho Indian Myths, by Aileen O'Bryan<br /> Dine Bahane': The Navajo Creation Story, by Paul G. Zolbrod<br /> <br /> I suspect you will need to go to such source material, since I haven't seen anything written up for Scion yet and I keep an eye out for such things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26114-muskrat","name":"Muskrat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-28T08:59:05-07:00","id":1495749,"title":"","content":"FWIW, the devs had wanted to do an official one. If I remember right, tribal authorities politely declined to share information, out of concerns for cultural misrepresentation/poor representation. And, frankly, I don't think I can blame them. <br /> <br /> Something to keep in mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12628-yukikaze","name":"yukikaze","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-28T15:14:50-07:00","id":1495787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>yukikaze</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1495478-help-with-a-navajo-pantheon?p=1495749#post1495749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">FWIW, the devs had wanted to do an official one. If I remember right, tribal authorities politely declined to share information, out of concerns for cultural misrepresentation/poor representation. And, frankly, I don't think I can blame them. <br /> <br /> Something to keep in mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>However, that would have been in an open source. A book that people would read without knowing the actual faith. A private game at home wouldn't risk the same disrespect. <br /> <br /> Mythology often is at odds with religion. Hera in myth is a mean spirited jerk. Hera in ancient Greek religion was a wise and gentle guide and authority. I could see a Navajo shaman (likely not the right term) knowing about such things. The Navajo are quick to study other cultures and faiths. Seeing the ways the Loa and Orishas are misrepresented in popular culture could be chilling to someone like that. <br /> <br /> A surprisingly large portion of Navajo tribal leaders read Latin and Greek. They would know the difference between the Greco Roman gods in myth and in faith. They'd be very unlikely to want something like that to befall their gods.<br /> <br /> A private game document wouldn't risk what the Navajo elders fear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-28T17:08:07-07:00","id":1495793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1495478-help-with-a-navajo-pantheon?p=1495787#post1495787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could see a Navajo shaman (likely not the right term) knowing about such things.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Hataalii </b>(or alternately <i>Yataalii</i>) translates to &quot;Singer&quot; with Dine spiritual medicine referred to in English as Sings. These range from short personal rituals to incredibly detailed songs/chants that can go on for several days, frequently also involving family members, friends, and neighbors as a communal effort to help the person the Sing is for to become spiritually healthy and back in synch with Dine society. This can be because of exposure to witchcraft, coming back from war, or any of a dozen other reasons. These songs are so complicated that some hataalii will only fully learn a few of them in their lifetime.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":12890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","user":"No One of Consequence","date":". 10-28-2022, 08:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-29T00:46:02-07:00","id":1495807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1495478-help-with-a-navajo-pantheon?p=1495793#post1495793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Hataalii </b>(or alternately <i>Yataalii</i>) translates to &amp;quot;Singer&amp;quot; with Dine spiritual medicine referred to in English as Sings. These range from short personal rituals to incredibly detailed songs/chants that can go on for several days, frequently also involving family members, friends, and neighbors as a communal effort to help the person the Sing is for to become spiritually healthy and back in synch with Dine society. This can be because of exposure to witchcraft, coming back from war, or any of a dozen other reasons. These songs are so complicated that some hataalii will only fully learn a few of them in their lifetime.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you. I hope to remember that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}